    "description": "An operations dashboard renders live fleet telemetry: 40 widgets over a WebSocket feed, user-selected filters, drill-down panels and a per-widget refresh cadence. Today each widget component stores its own copy of the filter state in local component state, formats numbers inside the template, and re-renders the whole tree on every tick; two panels disagree after a filter change and the charts flicker under load. The team wants presentation state to live in one place per view, to be derived from the model rather than duplicated, and to be observable so a template can bind to it without formatting or fetching logic. Designers also want the same state shape reused for a future mobile view. The decision to implement: how view state is represented and bound so templates stay declarative and multiple views share one state representation.",
    "decision_statement": "Represent view state once and bind templates to it declaratively so multiple views share one representation.",
    "notes": "Holdout family: presentation-model is the acceptable sibling when the reviewer avoids the VM framing."
  },
